-- חוזר לבעלויות תש"ע/4: ניכוי שכר מעובדי הוראה בשל שביתות/עיצומים במערכת
-- החינוך בשנת הלימודים התש"ע
-- Deducting the salary of teaching staff who took part in the strikes and
-- sanctions of June 2010: the owners' duty to deduct, the two scales of
-- deduction under the takanon's rule on unjustified absence (section 1.25.14),
-- and the Ministry's deduction from its payments to the owners.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `תש"ע/4 ניכוי שכר מעובדי הוראה בשל שביתות/עיצומים`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, date (5.7.2010), addressee, greeting and subject line; the operative paragraphs that follow them are encoded below.

-- akn:preamble/p12 The facts: from June 2010 the secondary teachers' organisation took strike action and sanctions in the secondary schools and seminaries; no rule of its own.

@desc A striking teacher's month, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `strike month` HAS
    `took part in the strike or sanctions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `absence share`                        IS A NUMBER @desc the month's unjustified absence as a share of the teacher's fixed work quota (0.1 = 10%)
    `pay for actual working hours`         IS A NUMBER @desc the month's pay for the hours the fixed timetable sets, shekels
    `pay for education and matriculation-preparation hours` IS A NUMBER @desc shekels a month
    `percentage additions for roles`       IS A NUMBER @desc shekels a month

DECLARE `strike action` IS ONE OF
    `deduct from the salary` HAS `amount deducted` IS A NUMBER
    `deduct from the owner's payments` HAS `amount withheld` IS A NUMBER

-- "יש לנכות משכרם של כל המורים שנטלו חלק … בהתאם לימים ולשעות": the
-- salary of every teacher who took part is deducted by the days and hours
-- of their part, by the takanon's rule on unjustified absence (section
-- 1.25.14), restated in sections 1 and 2. No deadline is printed, so the
-- duty has none.
@ref akn:preamble/p13 akn:preamble/p14
GIVEN s IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `deducting for the strike` s IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `deduct from the salary` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` EQUALS `the strike deduction` s
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "the salary of every teacher who took part is deducted for the days and hours of the strike"

§§ `1`

-- Section 1: where the month's absence is less than 10% of the teacher's
-- fixed work quota, the offset is from the actual working hours only, not
-- from the education or matriculation-preparation hours or the percentage
-- additions for roles.
@ref akn:art_1
GIVEN s IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the deduction under section 1` s IS
    s's `absence share` TIMES s's `pay for actual working hours`

GIVEN s IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1 governs` s IF
    s's `absence share` LESS THAN 0.1

§§ `2`

-- Section 2: where the absence exceeds 10%, the proportional part of the
-- unjustified absence is offset also from the education and matriculation
-- hours and from the percentage additions for roles.
@ref akn:art_2
GIVEN s IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the deduction under section 2` s IS
    s's `absence share`
    TIMES (    s's `pay for actual working hours`
          PLUS s's `pay for education and matriculation-preparation hours`
          PLUS s's `percentage additions for roles`)

GIVEN s IS A `strike month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 2 governs` s IF
    s's `absence share` GREATER THAN 0.1

-- "על הבעלות לנכות שכר מהעובד לפי מערכת השעות הקבועה של המורה בביה"ס": the
-- owner deducts by the teacher's fixed timetable at the school, so the
-- absence share is the hours of that timetable missed.
@ref akn:art_2/p2
GIVEN `hours of the fixed timetable missed` IS A NUMBER
      `hours of the fixed timetable` IS A NUMBER @desc the teacher's fixed weekly timetable at the school, for the month
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the absence share by the fixed timetable` `hours of the fixed timetable missed` `hours of the fixed timetable` IS
    IF `hours of the fixed timetable` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `hours of the fixed timetable missed` DIVIDED BY `hours of the fixed timetable`
    ELSE 0

-- "משרד החינוך ינכה מתשלומי המת"מ השוטפים לבעלויות": the Ministry deducts
-- from its current payments to the owners, by the hours budgeted in the
-- striking institutions and the dates of the strike. No deadline is
-- printed, so the duty has none.
@ref akn:art_2/p3
GIVEN `budgeted hours in the striking institutions` IS A NUMBER
      `budgeted value of an hour on the strike dates` IS A NUMBER @desc shekels; set by the Ministry's budgeting
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `the Ministry's deduction from the owner` `budgeted hours in the striking institutions` `budgeted value of an hour on the strike dates` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `deduct from the owner's payments` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` EQUALS `budgeted hours in the striking institutions` TIMES `budgeted value of an hour on the strike dates`
    LEST BREACH BY `the Ministry of Education` BECAUSE "section 2: the Ministry deducts from its current payments to the owners for the budgeted hours on the strike dates"

§§ `The month's deduction`

-- The reading adopted (F-2009-10_tasha_04-a): the wider deduction needs
-- absence that EXCEEDS 10%, so 10% exactly is deducted under section 1.
@export default The salary deducted from a teaching employee for a month of the 2010 strike or sanctions under circular תש"ע/4
GIVEN s IS A `strike month` @desc the teacher's month
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the strike deduction` s IS
    IF s's `took part in the strike or sanctions`
    THEN IF `section 2 governs` s
         THEN `the deduction under section 2` s
         ELSE `the deduction under section 1` s
    ELSE 0

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- F-2009-10_tasha_04-a: absence of exactly 10% is neither "less than 10%"
-- (section 1) nor "more than 10%" (section 2).
`a month with exactly 10% absence` MEANS
    `strike month` WITH
        `took part in the strike or sanctions` IS TRUE
        `absence share`                        IS 0.1
        `pay for actual working hours`         IS 8000
        `pay for education and matriculation-preparation hours` IS 1000
        `percentage additions for roles`       IS 1000

`neither section governs exactly 10%` MEANS
        (NOT `section 1 governs` `a month with exactly 10% absence`)
    AND (NOT `section 2 governs` `a month with exactly 10% absence`)
#ASSERT `neither section governs exactly 10%`

-- The pay figures are round placeholders.
`a month with 5% absence` MEANS
    `strike month` WITH
        `took part in the strike or sanctions` IS TRUE
        `absence share`                        IS 0.05
        `pay for actual working hours`         IS 8000
        `pay for education and matriculation-preparation hours` IS 1000
        `percentage additions for roles`       IS 1000

`a month with 20% absence` MEANS
    `strike month` WITH
        `took part in the strike or sanctions` IS TRUE
        `absence share`                        IS 0.2
        `pay for actual working hours`         IS 8000
        `pay for education and matriculation-preparation hours` IS 1000
        `percentage additions for roles`       IS 1000

#ASSERT `the strike deduction` `a month with 5% absence` EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `the strike deduction` `a month with 20% absence` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `the strike deduction` `a month with exactly 10% absence` EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `the absence share by the fixed timetable` 4 40 EQUALS 0.1

#TRACE `deducting for the strike` `a month with 20% absence` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `deduct from the salary` 2000 AT 1
-- Deducting the wrong amount does not discharge the duty: it stays owed.
#TRACE `deducting for the strike` `a month with 20% absence` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `deduct from the salary` 1600 AT 1
